opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Virtual package for the C++ compiler, which zcaml provides as zig c++"
description: """
zcaml compiles C++ with `zig c++`, so no separate system C++ compiler is
needed. Unlike conf-c++, which runs the build machine's `c++`, this package is
an empty check: it succeeds because the toolchain already has one."""
maintainer: "David Allsopp <dra27@dra27.uk>"
authors: "David Allsopp"
homepage: "https://github.com/ocaml/opam-repository"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/ocaml/opam-repository/issues"
license: "CC0-1.0+"
build: []
flags: conf
